<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>The ratio in which a point divides a line</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(A({@A[1]@},\,{@A[2]@},\,{@A[3]@})\), \(B({@B[1]@},\,{@B[2]@},\,{@B[3]@})\) and \(P({@P[1]@},\,{@P[2]@},\,{@P[3]@})\) lie on one straight line.</p><div>(a) P divides AB [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) \(AP : PB =\) [[input:ans2]] \(:\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>Give the ratio in whole numbers.</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\overrightarrow{AB} = {@cv3(AB)@}\) and \(\overrightarrow{AP} = {@cv3(AP)@} = {@t@}\,\overrightarrow{AB}\).</p><p>(a) [[if test="is(fl = 1)"]]\(t = {@t@}\) is between 0 and 1, so P is between A and B: P divides AB internally.[[else]]\(t = {@t@}\) is [[if test="is(t > 1)"]]greater than 1[[else]]negative[[/if]], so P is outside the segment AB: P divides AB externally.[[/if]]</p><p>(b) \(\overrightarrow{PB} = {@cv3(PB)@}\), which is \({@1-t@}\,\overrightarrow{AB}\). So the lengths are in the ratio \(AP : PB = {@abs(t)@} : {@abs(1-t)@} = {@m@} : {@n@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[cv3(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]],[v[3]]);
/* Design: the ratio in which a point divides a line. Five internal, five external; t = AP/AB is shown in feedback (it is not an answer). Source: original. */
plist: [[[2,1,1],[11,7,-8],[5,3,-2],1,2,1],[[-3,-2,5],[-11,6,9],[-9,4,8],3,1,1],[[1,-1,-4],[-4,9,-9],[-1,3,-6],2,3,1],[[0,0,-3],[4,-8,-7],[1,-2,-4],1,3,1],[[-2,3,-1],[8,13,-16],[4,9,-10],3,2,1],[[-4,1,-2],[-2,-1,4],[-1,-2,7],3,1,0],[[-3,-4,-2],[3,2,-8],[-6,-7,1],1,3,0],[[0,3,-2],[-6,9,7],[-10,13,13],5,2,0],[[-5,-1,-1],[-14,5,8],[1,-5,-7],2,5,0],[[-2,-4,-3],[1,-10,-9],[2,-12,-11],4,1,0]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
A: plist[ix][1]; B: plist[ix][2]; P: plist[ix][3]; m: plist[ix][4]; n: plist[ix][5]; fl: plist[ix][6];
t: (P[1]-A[1])/(B[1]-A[1]);
den: if fl = 1 then m+n else abs(m-n);
opts: [["int", is(fl=1), "internally"], ["ext", is(fl=0), "externally"]];
ta1: first(mcq_correct(opts)); wa1: first(mcq_incorrect(opts));
AP: P-A; AB: B-A; PB: B-P;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
